============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-space along which Ke is preserved.
  Physically: simultaneous rescaling of variables that keeps the physics invariant.

  Generator 1:
    etaP x exp(+0.142*eps), Vs x exp(+0.986*eps), alpha x exp(+0.063*eps)
    Meaning: increase Vs while increase etaP, increase alpha
             to keep Ke (and e*) unchanged

  Generator 2:
    etaP x exp(+0.201*eps), r0 x exp(+0.972*eps), alpha x exp(+0.089*eps), rho x exp(+0.066*eps)
    Meaning: increase r0 while increase etaP, increase alpha, increase rho
             to keep Ke (and e*) unchanged

  Generator 3:
    etaP x exp(-0.628*eps), Vs x exp(+0.063*eps), r0 x exp(+0.089*eps), alpha x exp(+0.723*eps), rho x exp(-0.205*eps), cp x exp(+0.141*eps), Tl-T0 x exp(+0.096*eps)
    Meaning: increase alpha while decrease etaP, increase Vs, increase r0, decrease rho, increase cp, increase Tl-T0
             to keep Ke (and e*) unchanged

  Generator 4:
    etaP x exp(-0.464*eps), r0 x exp(+0.066*eps), alpha x exp(-0.205*eps), rho x exp(+0.849*eps), cp x exp(+0.104*eps), Tl-T0 x exp(+0.071*eps)
    Meaning: increase rho while decrease etaP, increase r0, decrease alpha, increase cp, increase Tl-T0
             to keep Ke (and e*) unchanged

  Generator 5:
    etaP x exp(+0.319*eps), alpha x exp(+0.141*eps), rho x exp(+0.104*eps), cp x exp(+0.928*eps)
    Meaning: increase cp while increase etaP, increase alpha, increase rho
             to keep Ke (and e*) unchanged

  Generator 6:
    etaP x exp(+0.218*eps), alpha x exp(+0.096*eps), rho x exp(+0.071*eps), Tl-T0 x exp(+0.967*eps)
    Meaning: increase Tl-T0 while increase etaP, increase alpha, increase rho
             to keep Ke (and e*) unchanged


